    "name": "count-max-the-window-parameter-picks-the-period-or-the-week",
    "why": "The `window` parameter is owner decision K's other half — period or week, and no `day` — and a type that resolved it once and hardcoded either reading is green on every fixture carrying only one condition. Two conditions run over one world: a weekly cap of two, breached by three duties in the first week, and a period cap of three, breached by the same person's four duties across the whole block. Hardcoding 'period' moves the weekly violation onto the block's dates; hardcoding 'week' makes the period violation disappear entirely, because neither week reaches four. Each direction of the mistake is caught by one of the two rows.",
